cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this release, please cite the companion tutorial paper below
  and the archived release, and cite UWB-ASC for the measured sessions (see
  references). The code is licensed under MIT, and everything under Data/,
  Code/methods/results/ and docs/, the literature record included, under
  CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-CODE and LICENSE-DATA).
title: "radiocal: reference implementations and result tables for infrastructure self-calibration"
abstract: >-
  The release of the tutorial "A Tutorial on Infrastructure Self-Calibration
  for Radio-Based Indoor Positioning". It holds the reference implementations
  of the tutorial's engines with their driver, the result tables of its
  examples, the record of its literature search, and a copy of the measured
  sessions of the UWB Anchor Self-Calibration Dataset (UWB-ASC) and of its
  code. The implementations are a closed form, multidimensional scaling, a
  factor graph, also with anchor priors and with range-offset states, an
  extended Kalman filter (EKF), a particle filter, a grid filter, and EKF and
  factor-graph estimators of simultaneous localization and mapping (SLAM),
  with shared robust kernels and one noise scale per session. The driver runs
  each implementation on the topology views it applies to, and a runner
  evaluates public range recordings that the readers of UWB-ASC convert. A
  regression gate and the pinned environment of the result tables come with
  them. The data descriptor of UWB-ASC documents the deployments and their
  ground truth, and UWB-ASC's Zenodo record
  (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24055896) archives the sessions, the raw
  recordings and the scripts that rebuild the sessions.
type: software
